@startuml CryptoWeb-E3-mvc-identitykyc
title CryptoWeb - Authentication and KYC (MVC view)

!theme plain
top to bottom direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 75
skinparam ranksep 90
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
hide circle


package "React views" {
  class "Login" as LV <<React view>> {
    +Login()
  }
  class "Register" as RV <<React view>> {
    +Register()
  }
  class "Kyc" as KV <<React view>> {
    +Kyc()
  }
  class "KycManagement" as AV <<React admin view>> {
    +KycManagement()
  }
}

package "Client adapters" {
  class "authApi" as AA <<API object>> {
    +login()
    +register()
    +getMe()
    +logout()
  }
  class "kycApi" as KA <<API object>> {
    +submit()
    +getStatus()
    +review()
    +listApplications()
  }
}

package "Express controllers and services" {
  class "Auth Controller" as AC <<controller module>> {
    +register()
    +login()
    +refresh()
    +logout()
  }
  class "KYC Controller" as KC <<controller module>> {
    +submit()
    +status()
    +review()
  }
  class "Auth Service" as AS <<service module>> {
    +register()
    +login()
    +refreshSession()
  }
  class "KYC Service" as KS <<service module>> {
    +submitKyc()
    +reviewKyc()
  }
}

package "MySQL entities" {
  class "User record" as U <<SQL entity>> {
    +id
    +email
    +role
  }
  class "KYC application record" as K <<SQL entity>> {
    +id
    +user_id
    +status
  }
}

LV ..> AA
RV ..> AA
KV ..> KA
AV ..> KA
AA ..> AC : REST
KA ..> KC : REST
AC ..> AS
KC ..> KS
AS ..> U : SQL
KS ..> K : SQL

legend bottom
React components are functional views; Express controllers and services remain modules.
endlegend

@enduml
